From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x1000: h2boot: go back to the previous kernel when an update's won't start (Eros Q)

An update over Wi-Fi keeps the kernel it replaces as /uImage.prev and its
Wi-Fi modules as /fathom/wifi/modules.prev, and leaves /fathom/boot-new.
Before loading /uImage, boot_linux() moves that marker on (boot-new,
boot-try1, boot-try2; the player deletes it once it's up): a third start
that still finds boot-try2 puts the previous kernel and modules back in
place, the new ones kept as .failed, and leaves /fathom/boot-fell-back for
the player to say so. A /uImage that won't load at all goes back at once.
Cards without the markers (copied by hand) start /uImage as before.

The code is Fathom's bootloader/fathom/bootpick.c (tested on the host by
tests/test_bootpick.c), which bootloader/build.sh copies into
bootloader/x1000/.
---
--- a/bootloader/SOURCES	2026-11-18 14:47:07
+++ b/bootloader/SOURCES	2026-11-18 14:47:20
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@
 #if defined(EROS_QN)
 x1000/fwcopy.c
 x1000/fwcopy-h2boot.c
+x1000/bootpick.c
 #endif
 #elif defined(HIBY_R1_NATIVE)
 ingenic/gui-ingenic.c
--- a/bootloader/x1000/boot.c	2026-11-18 14:47:03
+++ b/bootloader/x1000/boot.c	2026-11-18 14:47:20
@@ -27,6 +27,9 @@
 #include "file.h"
 #include "linuxboot.h"
 #include "boot-x1000.h"
+#if defined(EROS_QN)
+#include "bootpick.h"
+#endif
 #include <ctype.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #if defined(EROS_QN)
@@ -134,10 +137,18 @@
      * the stock system in the flash, if it isn't there yet */
     fathom_copy_firmware(false);
     show_boot_logo();   /* Fathom: on screen while the kernel loads */
+    /* Fathom: an update's kernel gets two starts to reach the player, then
+     * the one before it goes back in place (bootpick.c) */
+    int fell_back = check_disk(false) == DISK_PRESENT && fathom_boot_pick();
 #endif
     struct uimage_header uh;
     size_t img_length;
     int handle = load_uimage_file("/uImage", &uh, &img_length);
+#if defined(EROS_QN)
+    /* one that won't load at all: the one before it, at once */
+    if(handle < 0 && !fell_back && fathom_boot_fall_back() == 0)
+        handle = load_uimage_file("/uImage", &uh, &img_length);
+#endif
     if(handle < 0)
         return;
 
